An `lb_retry_match` expression now only counts as a response condition if it mentions a reverse-proxy placeholder. A request-only expression like `{http.request.method} == "POST"` no longer makes successful responses retryable. Instead it goes back to restricting which failed requests may be retried. I haven't run this against your reproduction or added a test.

The check is a plain substring search on the expression text, not a full parse. It treats an expression as a response condition if it contains `{rp.` or `http.reverse_proxy.`. I matched the long form too because the Caddyfile may expand `{rp.*}` before the expression reaches the handler. Matching on `http.reverse_proxy.` also covers placeholders written directly in CEL as `ph(req, "http.reverse_proxy...")`.

One side effect: expressions using `{http.reverse_proxy.upstream.*}`, which are set before the round-trip, are also treated as response conditions. That matches the previous behaviour for those expressions, so nothing changes for them.

