After the round-trip, only expressions that mention a reverse_proxy placeholder are evaluated against the response. The fix is in `matcherSetHasExpressionMatcher` in `modules/caddyhttp/reverseproxy/reverseproxy.go`. It now looks for `http.reverse_proxy.` or `{rp.` in the expression text; the full form is what Caddyfile configs normally contain once adapted.

Other expressions, like the `{http.request.method} == "POST"` example in the issue, go back to their earlier meaning. They only decide whether a failed round-trip may be retried, so a successful response is passed straight through.

**Decision for you:** the check is plain text matching on the expression. It will treat any reference to a reverse_proxy placeholder as a response condition, including `{rp.is_transport_error}`. That flag isn't set at this point, so it is presumably empty and the condition won't match. Stricter parsing of the expression would avoid this, but it's more code than this fix needs.

