Request-only `lb_retry_match` expressions no longer cause successful responses to be retried. Only expressions that reference upstream response placeholders are now checked against the response. I haven't run the change or written a test for it.

- **Response conditions:** an expression counts as one only if it uses a status code, status text or response header placeholder. Both the `{rp.*}` shorthand and the full `{http.reverse_proxy.*}` form are recognised.
- **Other expressions:** anything else, like `{http.request.method} == "POST"`, goes back to its pre-v2.11.3 meaning. It only decides which requests may be retried after a failed round-trip.

The match is a plain substring check on the expression text. A response placeholder name appearing inside a string literal would also be treated as a response condition.

